      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're correct that pandas is concerned about modifying the original DataFrame. When working with data that might have side effects or unintended behavior, the `.copy()` method is generally safer to avoid potential issues. `.loc` works the same way, returning a view of the original DataFrame, so using `.copy()` is the standard way to avoid the warning and ensure the original data remains intact in a production pipeline.",
